# Asset pipeline environment. Copy this file to tools/asset_pipeline/.env (git-ignored) and fill in
# what you use. Every line is KEY=VALUE; blank lines and # comments are ignored; surrounding quotes
# are stripped. Everything after the = is the value, so do not put a comment on a KEY= line. A
# variable already set in the shell wins over this file. Paths use forward slashes, also on Windows.
# Nothing here is required: with no keys and no tools the mock providers still work.
# `uv run asset doctor` reports which of these are set and whether the tools are the pinned versions.

# ---- Image generation (concept, turnaround). Set the key for the provider you select in
# providers.local.yaml (or pass --image-provider). One key per provider.

# Google: providers `google` (Nano Banana) and `google-pro` (Gemini 3 Pro Image).
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# OpenAI: provider `openai` (GPT Image).
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# fal.ai: provider `fal` (FLUX etc.), and the `trellis` / `trellis-multi` 3D providers.
FAL_KEY=

# ---- Image-to-3D (to3d). One key per provider you want in the bake-off. TRELLIS.2 uses FAL_KEY.

# Tripo: provider `tripo`.
TRIPO_API_KEY=
# Meshy: provider `meshy`.
MESHY_API_KEY=
# Hyper3D Rodin: provider `rodin`.
RODIN_API_KEY=

# ---- Prompt writer (concept prompts, brief).

# Provider `anthropic-api` (Messages API, API billing). Not needed for `claude-cli`.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional: alternative Messages API endpoint for `anthropic-api`.
#ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=
# Provider `claude-cli`: path to the `claude` binary if it is not on PATH. It uses your Claude Code
# login, or CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, both read by `claude` itself, never by the pipeline.
#ASSET_CLAUDE_BIN=

# ---- Tools. Versions are pinned in versions.yaml; `doctor` checks them.

# Path to Godot 4.7.2 standard (non-.NET) if `godot` is not on PATH.
#GODOT=
# Path to Blender 4.5 LTS if `blender` is not on PATH (native runner).
#ASSET_BLENDER_BIN=
# native | docker | auto (default auto: a local Blender wins, else Docker).
#ASSET_BLENDER_RUNNER=
# Override the Docker image name (default silent-water/blender-cleanup:<version>).
#ASSET_BLENDER_IMAGE=

# ---- Paths and output.

# Where `godot-check` writes renders and Godot logs (default ./logs; --log-dir overrides).
#LOG_DIR=
# Repo root override (default: the nearest parent holding project.godot).
#ASSET_PIPELINE_ROOT=
# Alternative path for providers.local.yaml (used by the tests).
#ASSET_PROVIDERS_LOCAL=
# If unset on Linux, `godot-check` renders under xvfb-run when it is installed.
#DISPLAY=

# ---- Not read from this file: the GitHub Projects MCP server in .mcp.json reads GITHUB_MCP_PAT from
# the shell that starts Claude Code (a fine-grained PAT with Projects read/write and Issues access).
